DevOps Architect Interview – Harman Group

Round 1 – Infrastructure & Kubernetes thinking

• Design a multi-tenant Kubernetes cluster with isolation across environments.
• Manage multiple Kustomize overlays without configuration drift.
• Terraform state got corrupted during backend migration. What is your recovery strategy?
• Perform zero-downtime upgrades for a stateful workload using Helm.
• Prevent lateral movement between pods inside a cluster.
• Your team wants custom AMIs for nodes. What checks happen before production?

⸻

Round 2 – Production debugging scenarios

• TLS handshakes start failing after an ALB config change. Trace the RCA.
• Nodes are healthy but kubectl logs returns nothing. What could cause this?
• Deploy a logging sidecar and CPU throttling spikes. What’s happening?
• Autoscaling isn’t triggering despite high CPU. Metrics, HPA, or API issue?
• Users see 504 errors but LB health checks are green. Where do you investigate?
• A production pod is OOMKilled but logs are missing. How do you debug?

⸻

Round 3 – Architecture & engineering thinking

• How do you design infrastructure that empowers developers but prevents misuse?
• What checks do you perform before approving a custom AMI to production?
• Observability architecture change — what trade-offs do you consider?
